---
// Source -> DAC -> Amp -> Headphone: where a DAC sits and why one dongle usually covers it. Static
// teaching diagram for the DAC article.
---

<figure class="fig">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 216" role="img" aria-label="A signal chain: source to DAC to amplifier to headphone, with a bracket showing a dongle combines the DAC and amp.">
    <defs>
      <marker id="ar" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto">
        <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="#FF9E2C"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- boxes -->
    <g>
      <rect x="30" y="54" width="150" height="78" rx="10" fill="#26292d" stroke="#34383d"></rect>
      <rect x="216" y="54" width="150" height="78" rx="10" fill="#26292d" stroke="#FF9E2C" stroke-opacity="0.55"></rect>
      <rect x="402" y="54" width="150" height="78" rx="10" fill="#26292d" stroke="#FF9E2C" stroke-opacity="0.55"></rect>
      <rect x="588" y="54" width="142" height="78" rx="10" fill="#26292d" stroke="#34383d"></rect>
    </g>

    <!-- box labels -->
    <g text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--mono)">
      <text x="105" y="88" font-size="15" fill="#e8ebed">SOURCE</text>
      <text x="105" y="108" font-size="10.5" fill="#565b60">phone · laptop</text>
      <text x="291" y="88" font-size="15" fill="#e8ebed">DAC</text>
      <text x="291" y="108" font-size="10.5" fill="#565b60">digital → analog</text>
      <text x="477" y="88" font-size="15" fill="#e8ebed">AMP</text>
      <text x="477" y="108" font-size="10.5" fill="#565b60">adds power</text>
      <text x="659" y="88" font-size="15" fill="#e8ebed">HEADPHONE</text>
      <text x="659" y="108" font-size="10.5" fill="#565b60">you</text>
    </g>

    <!-- arrows + wire labels -->
    <g stroke="#FF9E2C" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#ar)">
      <line x1="182" y1="93" x2="212" y2="93"></line>
      <line x1="368" y1="93" x2="398" y2="93"></line>
      <line x1="554" y1="93" x2="584" y2="93"></line>
    </g>
    <g font-family="var(--mono)" font-size="9.5" fill="#FF9E2C" text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="197" y="80">digital</text>
      <text x="383" y="80">analog</text>
      <text x="569" y="80">louder</text>
    </g>

    <!-- bracket: dongle combines DAC + amp -->
    <path d="M216 150 L216 160 L552 160 L552 150" fill="none" stroke="#565b60" stroke-width="1"></path>
    <text x="384" y="182" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--mono)" font-size="11" fill="#868d92">a USB-C dongle / DAC-amp combines these</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    The DAC converts, the amp powers, the headphone plays. Every device already has a DAC &mdash; and one small
    dongle usually does both jobs, which is why you rarely think about them separately.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig {
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 18px 18px 14px;
  }
  .fig svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .fig figcaption {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--muted-2);
    font-family: var(--mono);
  }
</style>
